  "panels": [
    {
      "id": null,
      "key": "panelpane-80fdb4b3bab3c94c",
      "title": "Rule Priorities",
      "visualSettings": "{\"text\":{\"alignment\":\"left\",\"format\":\"markdown\"}}",
      "keepVisualSettingsConsistentWithParent": true,
      "panelType": "TextPanel",
      "text": "###Every Falco rule has a priority which indicates the triggered rule's severity.\n\n###The possible set of priorities are:\n\n   - EMERGENCY\n   - ALERT\n   - CRITICAL\n   - ERROR\n   - WARNING\n   - NOTICE\n   - INFORMATIONAL\n   - DEBUG\n\n###The general guidelines used to assign priorities to rules are the following:\n\n   - If a rule is related to a write state (e.g., filesystem activity), the priority is ERROR.\n   - If a rule is related to an unauthorized read state (e.g., reading sensitive files), the priority is WARNING.\n   - If a rule is related to unexpected behavior (e.g., spawning an unexpected shell in a container, opening an unexpected network connection, etc.), the priority is NOTICE.\n   - If a rule is related to behaving against good practices (e.g., unexpected privileged containers, containers with sensitive mounts, running interactive commands as root), the priority is INFO.\n   \nFor more information, see the official Falco documentation at https://falco.org/docs/.\n\n####Note: This dashboard relies on Falco. If the Dashboard is not populated, enable Falco by setting the flag \"falco:enabled\" as \"true\" in values.yaml as mentioned here: https://github.com/SumoLogic/sumologic-kubernetes-collection/blob/master/deploy/docs/Installation_with_Helm.md"
    },
    {
      "id": null,
      "key": "panelpane-2924e599a7a2cb4d",
      "title": "Total Events",
      "visualSettings": "{\"general\":{\"type\":\"svp\"},\"svp\":{\"label\":\"Event(s)\",\"noDataString\":\"0\"}}",
      "keepVisualSettingsConsistentWithParent": true,
      "panelType": "SumoSearchPanel",
      "queries": [
        {
          "transient": false,
          "queryString": "*falco* output_fields rule priority output\n| json  \"log.priority\" \n| count",
          "queryType": "Logs",
          "queryKey": "A",
          "metricsQueryMode": "Advanced",
          "metricsQueryData": {
            "metric": "",
            "aggregationType": "None",
            "groupBy": "",
            "filters": [],
            "operators": null
          },
          "tracesQueryData": null,
          "spansQueryData": null,
          "parseMode": "Manual",
          "timeSource": "Message",
